From: 3090 team <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: 2026-06-10
Subject: [PATCH] model loader: 480s -> 1800s unbalanced-load timeout (cold cache)

Graft of R9700's patch 048 (their numbering; finding 2026-06-10): big-model
TP=2 loads on a cold page cache exceed upstream's 480s
UNBALANCED_MODEL_LOADING_TIMEOUT_S rank-skew window — the slower rank gets
killed mid-load. Bites 30-62 GB checkpoints when NVMe is contended (e.g.
bake-off docker I/O); the timeout still catches genuinely wedged ranks.
v0.5.16 re-port: the constant moved verbatim from model_runner.py into the
new model_runner_components/load_model_utils.py (model_runner decomposition);
same one-line bump; v0.5.17 re-anchor (new maybe_precompile_model_kernels_after_loading below the constant). Narrative: patches/README.md.

diff --git a/python/sglang/srt/model_executor/model_runner_components/load_model_utils.py b/python/sglang/srt/model_executor/model_runner_components/load_model_utils.py
diff --git a/python/sglang/srt/model_executor/model_runner_components/load_model_utils.py b/python/sglang/srt/model_executor/model_runner_components/load_model_utils.py
index f3ada40..268ef73 100644
--- a/python/sglang/srt/model_executor/model_runner_components/load_model_utils.py
+++ b/python/sglang/srt/model_executor/model_runner_components/load_model_utils.py
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@ logger = logging.getLogger(__name__)
 _is_npu = is_npu()
 
 
-UNBALANCED_MODEL_LOADING_TIMEOUT_S = 480  # leave more time for post data processing
+UNBALANCED_MODEL_LOADING_TIMEOUT_S = 1800  # [3090 049] cold-page-cache TP2 loads of 30-62 GB checkpoints exceed upstream 480s rank-skew window (R9700 finding); leave more time for post data processing
 
 
